    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd Art 133 Head, §§6600, 6603, 6608, 6608-a & 6608-b, Ed L",
    "lawSection": "Education Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S4558\n\nSPONSOR: PARKER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the education law, in relation to\nregistered dental assisting\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill would change the title \"certified dental assistant\" to \"regis-\ntered dental assistant\".\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 changes the statutory article heading to include the profes-\nsion of registered dental assisting.\n\nSection 2 changes the coverage of Article 133 to include the profession\nof registered dental assisting.\n\nSection 3 changes the reference from \"certified dental assistant\" to\n\"registered dental assistant\".\n\nSection 4 changes the references from \"certified dental assistant\" to\n\"registered dental assistant\" and the references from \"dental assistant\"\nto \"registered dental assistant\".\n\nSection 5 changes the references from \"certified dental assistant\" to\n\"registered dental assistant\", clarifies that only a person licensed as\na registered dental assistant can practice the profession of registered\ndental assisting and use the title \"registered dental assistant\".\n\nSection 6 changes the references from \"certified dental assistant\" to\n\"registered dentalò assistant.\"\n\nSection 7 makes the bill effective immediately upon enactment into law.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill creates the new legally protected title of \"registered dental\nassistant\" and eliminates the old protected title of \"certified dental\nassistant\". The old title of \"certified dental assistant\" was causing\nconfusion between people certified by the New York State Education\nDepartment and people certified by the Dental Assisting National Board\n(DANB). This was leading to unintentional criminal violations for those\nwho illegally used the \"certified dental assistant\" title in New York\nwhen they possessed only DANB certification. Similarly, both dentists\nand the public were being confused by which certified dental assistants\nwere licensed by the State of New York and which were only DANE-certi-\nfied. This bill ends those problems by changing the protected title of\nthe profession and all concomitant references to \"regigtpdental assist-\nant\" and fully integrates the profession of regist'didd'dental assisting\ninto Article 133 of the Education Law.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2017-18: S9084 - passed Assembly, Referred to Rules\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately upon being enacted into law.\n",
